{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" | head -n 20; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" probes --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" fresh-rerun --help; rg --files \"$(dirname \"$STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT\")/frozen-inputs/coordinator-guidance\"'","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Run the pinned assessment helpers in their recorded Pixi environment.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nfrom contextlib import chdir, nullcontext\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport assessment_procedure as procedure\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n\n\ndef git(*args, cwd=ROOT):\n    return subprocess.check_output([\"git\", *args], cwd=cwd)\n\n\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: run_probes.py [-h] [-o OUTPUT] [--response RESPONSE]\n                     [--only {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]]\n                     [--skip {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]]\n                     [--check-remote] [--allow GLOB [GLOB ...]]\n                     [--kind {dataset,component,study,skill}] [--overwrite]\n                     [--quiet]\n                     path\n\nRun the STAMPED probes over a checked-out research object.\n\n    run_probes.py <path> [-o probes.json] [--response response.json]\n                  [--only NAME ...] [--skip NAME ...] [--check-remote]\n                  [--kind dataset|component|study|skill]\n\nWrites the per-probe results, and optionally a response JSON (the format in\n``../stamped-conventions/references/response-format.md``) in which every item a\nprobe speaks to carries that probe's verdict and every other item is left\n``not-checked`` for the assessing session to judge.\nWithout a Git commit, ``-o`` retains a limitation receipt and exit code 2;\nno response draft is produced.\n\nThe probes never modify the object.  Nothing here replaces the judgement items:\na response straight out of this script is a draft, not an assessment.\n\npositional arguments:\n  path                  checked-out object to probe\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  -o, --output OUTPUT   write the probe results here\n  --response RESPONSE   also write a draft response JSON here\n  --only {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]\n                        run just these probes\n  --skip {ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} [{ci-present,clone-weight,derived-have-records,entry-point,env-spec-tracked,inputs-untouched,large-in-annex,license-declared,modules-separated,no-abs-paths,platform-assumptions,run-env-linked,subdatasets-resolvable,tree-clean} ...]\n  --check-remote        contact submodule urls (network)\n  --allow GLOB [GLOB ...]\n                        paths no-abs-paths may skip, for files that genuinely\n                        have to carry a host path\n  --kind {dataset,component,study,skill}\n  --overwrite           replace an existing --response file instead of keeping\n                        its judged answers\n  --quiet\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py [-h]\n                          {items,validate,encode,decode,template,set,stamp,table} ...\n\nSTAMPED checklist responses: read the items, validate, encode, decode.\n\nThe vendored checklist in ``../checklist/`` is the only item source, and this\nscript is the only writer of a checklist-app URL.  See\n``../references/response-format.md`` for the response JSON and\n``../references/verdicts.md`` for the statuses.\n\nSubcommands\n-----------\nitems      list the pinned items (id, level, principle codes, text)\nset        answer one item in a response JSON, in place (what every run was\n           otherwise writing a merge script for)\ntable      the per-item markdown table response-format.md section 4 asks for\nstamp      fill harness, model, scope and kind; optionally hash a retained capture\nvalidate   check a response JSON against the pin and the app's constraints\nencode     response JSON -> checklist-app URL\ndecode     checklist-app URL -> response JSON (how a filled web form becomes\n           reference answers for calibration)\ntemplate   emit a response JSON skeleton with every item not-checked\n\nExit codes: 0 ok, 1 validation failed, 2 usage.\n\npositional arguments:\n  {items,validate,encode,decode,template,set,stamp,table}\n    items               list the pinned items\n    validate            check a response JSON\n    encode              response JSON -> URL\n    decode              URL -> response JSON\n    template            emit an all-not-checked response JSON\n    set                 answer one item in a response JSON, in place\n    stamp               fill harness, model, scope, kind and capture identity\n    table               print the per-item markdown table\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: assessment.py [-h] --path PATH --entry ENTRY\n                     --outputs OUTPUTS [OUTPUTS ...] --workdir WORKDIR\n                     -o OUTPUT [--rtol RTOL] [--timeout TIMEOUT]\n                     [--max-get-gb MAX_GET_GB] [--in-container IN_CONTAINER]\n\nReplay documented outputs from a verified complete copy, never from HEAD.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --path PATH\n  --entry ENTRY\n  --outputs OUTPUTS [OUTPUTS ...]\n  --workdir WORKDIR\n  -o, --output OUTPUT\n  --rtol RTOL\n  --timeout TIMEOUT\n  --max-get-gb MAX_GET_GB\n  --in-container IN_CONTAINER\n/Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-16-j01/attempt-01/frozen-inputs/coordinator-guidance/judging.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat \"$(dirname \"$STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT\")/frozen-inputs/coordinator-guidance/judging.md\"; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response stamp --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response template --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" validate --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" - \"$STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport hashlib,json,sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(sys.argv[1]); d=json.load(open(p)); print('manifest_file_sha256',hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()); print('head_commit',d.get('head_commit')); print('git_metadata',d.get('git_metadata')); print('workspace',d.get('workspace')); print('errors',d.get('errors')); print('omissions',d.get('omissions'))\nPY\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/report.md\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/analysis/group_analysis.py\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/analysis/restore_maps.py\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/input/upstream-methods.md\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'cat \"$(dirname \"$STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT\")/frozen-inputs/coordinator-guidance/judging.md\"; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response stamp --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response template --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" validate --help; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" - \"$STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport hashlib,json,sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path(sys.argv[1]); d=json.load(open(p)); print('manifest_file_sha256',hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()); print('head_commit',d.get('head_commit')); print('git_metadata',d.get('git_metadata')); print('workspace',d.get('workspace')); print('errors',d.get('errors')); print('omissions',d.get('omissions'))\nPY\ncat \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/report.md\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/analysis/group_analysis.py\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/analysis/restore_maps.py\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/input/upstream-methods.md\"'","aggregated_output":"# Scientific assessment context\n\nAssess the original NARPS Hypothesis 1: a positive parametric effect of potential gain in vmPFC for the equal-indifference group.\nThe original [analysis instructions](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf) require whole-brain-corrected inference.\nThe scientific task is in `input/study-task.md`.\n\nWorkers receive 54 participant gain-effect maps from team AO86 and the corresponding cohort metadata.\nPreprocessing and participant modeling are fixed; evaluate group inference conditional on those inputs.\nJudge whether the analysis handles the intended participants, image geometry, quality, gain scaling, uncertainty and anatomical interpretation appropriately.\nThe maps represent independent participants; runs have already been combined within each person.\nEvaluate exclusions, uncertainty and multiple-comparison correction against the actual method.\nDefensible approaches can reach different conclusions; matching a prior team's answer is not the criterion.\nKeep scientific validity separate from the frozen STAMPED assessment.\nCheck how image coverage and missing observations enter the analysis; whether spatial alignment, vmPFC definition, group-model assumptions and whole-brain correction support the claimed inference; and whether quality checks, uncertainty and figures make those decisions inspectable.\nDo not require a particular mask, atlas, model or numerical result.\nParticipant variance maps are absent; judge methods against the supplied data.\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py stamp [-h] [--harness HARNESS] [--model MODEL]\n                                [--scope SCOPE]\n                                [--kind {dataset,component,study,skill}]\n                                [--dependency DEPENDENCY] [--capture CAPTURE]\n                                response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --harness HARNESS     e.g. \"claude-code (subagent)\"\n  --model MODEL\n  --scope SCOPE         what this assessment did and did not cover\n  --kind {dataset,component,study,skill}\n                        the object's kind (see references/project-kinds.md)\n  --dependency DEPENDENCY\n                        e.g. \"stamped-conventions@0.1.0\"; repeatable\n  --capture CAPTURE     hash a retained delivery manifest/archive; preserve\n                        any recorded Git commit\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py template [-h] [-o OUTPUT]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help           show this help message and exit\n  -o, --output OUTPUT\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py validate [-h] response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\nmanifest_file_sha256 1bc0f46ef4ad58e9f70bb654d761eb330f15d1c87929ad165d414907dd7d0f68\nhead_commit 675620fed8a134102b1b07226fe39d67630ee6f7\ngit_metadata {'coverage': 'Exact workspace-resident Git bytes, modes and links; explicit dependencies separately declared', 'index': {'kind': 'file', 'mode': 420, 'path': 'content/workspace/.git/index', 'sha256': 'f851e036c272307d53eccf58eca1fcb5541c83d99868b000ccb945619a8adb69', 'size': 6095}, 'local_metadata_complete': True, 'retained_entries': 1050, 'root': 'content/workspace/.git', 'root_kind': 'directory'}\nworkspace content/workspace\nerrors []\nomissions []\n# Potential gains and brain activity\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe supplied equal-indifference group maps do **not support** the prediction of a positive vmPFC gain effect under whole-brain family-wise error control. No significant whole-brain voxel overlapped the prespecified anatomical vmPFC proxy (9 voxels survived whole-brain correction elsewhere). The proxy's mean participant-level gain-effect estimate was near zero, with a confidence interval spanning zero. This is a failure to find corrected evidence for the prediction, not evidence that the true effect is exactly zero.\n\n## Group analysis\n\nI analyzed all 54 equal-indifference participants with their unthresholded AO86 gain-effect COPE maps. The group model was a one-sample, voxelwise t test against zero (df=53), testing the predicted positive direction. The common analysis mask contained 210,968 voxels (nonzero coverage in at least 90% of maps). All maps matched the source manifest's byte counts and SHA-256 checksums, shared a voxel grid and affine, and contained only finite values; no participant was excluded.\n\nTo control family-wise error across the entire mask, I used Bonferroni correction over all 210,968 voxels at alpha=.05. This is conservative but controls FWE without relying on spatial-independence assumptions. Nine positive voxels survived (peak t(53)=6.62, uncorrected p=9.31×10⁻⁹; Bonferroni p=.00196; MNI x=-26, y=-102, z=-3.6 mm). They were in posterior/inferior locations, not the hypothesized vmPFC. The full corrected voxel table is in [`results/fwe_positive_voxels.csv`](results/fwe_positive_voxels.csv).\n\nI operationalized vmPFC using the Harvard–Oxford cortical atlas: Frontal Medial, Subcallosal, and Frontal Orbital parcels, limited to |MNI x|≤24 mm and z≤10 mm, resampled to the supplied map grid with nearest-neighbor interpolation. This broad atlas-derived mask is an anatomical proxy, not a unique definition of vmPFC; the atlas provides structural parcels rather than a functional boundary ([FSL atlas documentation](https://fsl.fmrib.ox.ac.uk/fsl/docs/other/datasets.html)). No corrected voxel fell in this proxy. As a descriptive secondary summary, the participant-average COPE in the proxy was 0.0002 (SD across participants=0.0816; 95% t interval [-0.0221, 0.0225]; t(53)=0.018, one-sided uncorrected p=.493). Leaving out one participant at a time moved the proxy mean between -0.0041 and 0.0030, so its sign was not robust to individual omission. This ROI summary is not the basis for the whole-brain decision.\n\n![Mean gain effect and whole-brain corrected positive voxels](figures/whole_brain_results.png)\n\n![Participant-level vmPFC proxy estimates](figures/vmPFC_proxy_participants.png)\n\n## Interpretation and limits\n\nThe supplied values are parameter estimates, not t or z statistics. AO86 mean-centered and variance-normalized the gain regressor before HRF convolution, so this contrast is not a response-per-currency-unit slope and cannot be converted to a monetary gain increment. It is conditional on AO86's separate gain/loss model and response-time-duration choice regressors. The group t model uses between-participant variability in these COPEs; participant variance maps were unavailable, so it cannot incorporate first-level uncertainty using a full weighted mixed-effects model. The results therefore concern the supplied model's group-average gain effect, not a model-independent causal response to cash amounts.\n\nThe 95% interval is compatible with small effects in either direction in the COPE scale. A null result after stringent whole-brain correction does not establish no vmPFC response; it means this analysis did not find sufficient corrected evidence that the mean effect is positive. The atlas proxy's borders and template differ slightly from the supplied MNI152NLin2009cAsym images, adding localization uncertainty. Bonferroni's conservatism also reduces sensitivity. The original NARPS instructions required whole-brain-corrected results for the binary hypothesis decision ([NARPS analysis instructions, Hypothesis 1](https://www.narps.info/files/narps_instructions_for_analysis_teams.pdf)).\n\n## Reproducibility\n\nThe initial workspace had 54 broken Git-annex pointers in `input/data/`, without accessible image bytes. I restored only the 54 exact COPE maps referenced by `input/sources.json` from its NeuroVault URLs and verified each downloaded file against the recorded size and SHA-256. No time-series scans were retrieved. To reproduce with the provided Python 3.13 environment:\n\n```bash\npython analysis/restore_maps.py\npython analysis/group_analysis.py\n```\n\nThe group script writes the statistical maps and summary to `results/`, the voxel and participant QC tables there, and the figures to `figures/`. Key numeric results are in [`results/summary.json`](results/summary.json); per-map checks are in [`results/map_qc.csv`](results/map_qc.csv). Analysis code is [`analysis/group_analysis.py`](analysis/group_analysis.py), and the map restoration/checksum code is [`analysis/restore_maps.py`](analysis/restore_maps.py).\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Group analysis of NARPS AO86 equal-indifference participant gain-effect maps.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json, hashlib\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport nibabel as nib\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom nilearn import datasets, image, plotting\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nIN=ROOT/'input'; OUT=ROOT/'results'; FIG=ROOT/'figures'\nOUT.mkdir(exist_ok=True); FIG.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nmeta=json.loads((IN/'sources.json').read_text())\nparticipants=pd.read_csv(IN/'participants.tsv',sep='\\t')\nparticipants=participants[participants.group=='equalIndifference'].copy()\nmanifest={Path(k).name:v for k,v in meta['files'].items() if k.startswith('data/')}\nassert len(participants)==54 and len(manifest)==54\n# Check IDs and byte checksums; maps are original unthresholded COPE images.\nparticipants['path']=participants.participant_id.map(lambda s: str(IN/'data'/f'{s}_hypo1_cope.nii.gz'))\nassert participants.path.notna().all()\nqc=[]; imgs=[]; arrays=[]; affine=None; shape=None\nfor r in participants.itertuples():\n    p=Path(r.path); m=manifest[p.name]; b=p.read_bytes()\n    assert len(b)==m['bytes'] and hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()==m['sha256'], p\n    im=nib.load(str(p)); a=im.get_fdata(dtype=np.float32)\n    if shape is None: shape=im.shape; affine=im.affine\n    assert im.shape==shape and np.allclose(im.affine,affine,atol=1e-5)\n    assert np.isfinite(a).all()\n    imgs.append(im); arrays.append(a)\n    qc.append({'participant_id':r.participant_id,'bytes':len(b),'sha256_verified':True,\n               'nonzero_voxels':int(np.count_nonzero(a)), 'min':float(a.min()),'max':float(a.max()),\n               'mean_nonzero':float(a[a!=0].mean()),'sd_nonzero':float(a[a!=0].std())})\npd.DataFrame(qc).to_csv(OUT/'map_qc.csv',index=False)\nY=np.stack(arrays,axis=0)\n# Common analysis domain: voxels nonzero (in-brain coverage) in >=90% maps.\nmask=(Y!=0).mean(axis=0)>=0.90\n# Ensure mask isn't influenced by a small number of coverage outliers; report domain details.\nN=Y.shape[0]; nvox=int(mask.sum())\nvals=Y[:,mask].astype(np.float64)\nmean=vals.mean(axis=0); sd=vals.std(axis=0,ddof=1); se=sd/np.sqrt(N)\nt=mean/se\np=stats.t.sf(t,N-1) # prespecified positive direction\np_bonf=np.minimum(p*nvox,1.)\nalpha=.05\nsig=(p_bonf<alpha)\n# Effect CI is on supplied standardized-regressor COPE units, not currency units.\ncrit=stats.t.ppf(.975,N-1)\nlow=mean-crit*se; high=mean+crit*se\n# Generate maps on common source grid.\ndef full_img(v, fill=0):\n    z=np.full(shape,fill,dtype=np.float32); z[mask]=v.astype(np.float32)\n    return nib.Nifti1Image(z,affine)\nmean_img=full_img(mean); t_img=full_img(t); p_img=full_img(-np.log10(np.maximum(p_bonf,1e-300)))\nmean_img.to_filename(OUT/'group_mean_cope.nii.gz')\nt_img.to_filename(OUT/'group_t_positive.nii.gz')\np_img.to_filename(OUT/'group_neglog10_p_bonferroni.nii.gz')\n# Harvard-Oxford cortical labels provide an independent anatomical reference. Use\n# medial frontal, subcallosal, and orbital frontal parcels as a broad vmPFC proxy.\natlas=datasets.fetch_atlas_harvard_oxford('cort-maxprob-thr25-2mm')\natlas_img=image.resample_to_img(atlas.maps,imgs[0],interpolation='nearest')\natlas_data=atlas_img.get_fdata().astype(int)\nlabels=list(atlas.labels)\nroi_names=['Frontal Medial Cortex','Subcallosal Cortex','Frontal Orbital Cortex']\nroi_ids=[labels.index(x) for x in roi_names]\ncoords=np.indices(shape); xcoord=coords[0]*affine[0,0]+affine[0,3]; zcoord=coords[2]*affine[2,2]+affine[2,3]\nroi=(np.isin(atlas_data,roi_ids)&(np.abs(xcoord)<=24)&(zcoord<=10)&mask)\n# ROI average is an interpretable secondary summary (not whole-brain corrected inference).\nroi_nvox=int(roi.sum()); roi_subj=Y[:,roi].mean(axis=1)\nroi_mean=float(roi_subj.mean()); roi_sd=float(roi_subj.std(ddof=1)); roi_se=roi_sd/np.sqrt(N)\nroi_t=roi_mean/roi_se; roi_p=float(stats.t.sf(roi_t,N-1))\nroi_ci=(roi_mean-crit*roi_se,roi_mean+crit*roi_se)\n# ROI based sensitivity leave-one-out range.\nloo=np.array([np.delete(roi_subj,i).mean() for i in range(N)])\n# QC summary and stats\nqcs=pd.DataFrame(qc)\nsummary={\n 'n_participants':N,'excluded':[],'shape':list(shape),'nvox_common_mask':nvox,\n 'mask_definition':'voxels with nonzero values in >=90% of the 54 images',\n 'mask_voxelwise_finite_all':bool(np.isfinite(vals).all()),\n 'whole_brain_model':'one-sample voxelwise t-test of unthresholded COPEs against 0; one-sided positive; df=53',\n 'correction':'Bonferroni family-wise error correction across all common-mask voxels; alpha=.05',\n 'n_fwe_significant_voxels':int(sig.sum()),\n 'n_fwe_significant_voxels_in_vmPFC_proxy':int(np.sum(sig & roi[mask])),\n 'peak_t':float(t.max()),'peak_coordinate_ijk':[int(q) for q in np.argwhere(mask)[np.argmax(t)]],\n 'peak_mni_xyz_mm':nib.affines.apply_affine(affine,np.argwhere(mask)[np.argmax(t)]).tolist(),\n 'peak_p_uncorrected':float(p.min()),'peak_p_bonferroni':float(p_bonf.min()),\n 'mean_significant_voxel_cope':float(mean[sig].mean()) if sig.any() else None,\n 'vmPFC_proxy_atlas':'Harvard-Oxford cortical atlas (25% max-probability): Frontal Medial, Subcallosal, Frontal Orbital parcels, restricted to |MNI x| <= 24 mm and z <= 10 mm; resampled nearest-neighbour to source grid',\n 'vmPFC_proxy_nvox':roi_nvox,'vmPFC_proxy_mean_cope':roi_mean,'vmPFC_proxy_sd_between_subject':roi_sd,\n 'vmPFC_proxy_ci95':[float(x) for x in roi_ci],'vmPFC_proxy_t':float(roi_t),'vmPFC_proxy_df':N-1,\n 'vmPFC_proxy_p_one_sided_uncorrected':roi_p,'vmPFC_proxy_leave_one_out_mean_range':[float(loo.min()),float(loo.max())],\n 'mean_image_mean_inside_mask':float(mean.mean()),'mean_within_subject_nonzero_cope_range':[float(Y.min()),float(Y.max())],\n 'all_maps_verified_against_sha256':True}\n(OUT/'summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))\n# Save participant-level ROI estimates and the corrected voxel coordinates.\nvol_idx=np.argwhere(mask)\nrows=[]\nfor j in np.where(sig)[0]:\n    ijk=vol_idx[j]; rows.append({'i':int(ijk[0]),'j':int(ijk[1]),'k':int(ijk[2]),\n        'x_mm':float(nib.affines.apply_affine(affine,ijk)[0]),'y_mm':float(nib.affines.apply_affine(affine,ijk)[1]),\n        'z_mm':float(nib.affines.apply_affine(affine,ijk)[2]),'mean_cope':float(mean[j]),'t':float(t[j]),\n        'p_uncorrected':float(p[j]),'p_bonferroni':float(p_bonf[j]),'in_vmPFC_proxy':bool(roi[tuple(ijk)])})\npd.DataFrame(rows).to_csv(OUT/'fwe_positive_voxels.csv',index=False)\n# Save participant-level ROI estimates and per-voxel table.\npd.DataFrame({'participant_id':participants.participant_id,'vmPFC_proxy_mean_cope':roi_subj}).to_csv(OUT/'vmPFC_proxy_participant_estimates.csv',index=False)\n# Figure 1: spatial mean and corrected positive voxels in separate, readable montages.\nplotting.plot_stat_map(mean_img,display_mode='z',cut_coords=[-8,-4,0,4],threshold=0,cmap='cold_hot',\n                       colorbar=True,vmax=.15,symmetric_cbar=True,title='Mean gain-effect COPE (N=54)',\n                       output_file=str(FIG/'group_mean_cope.png'))\nsigvals=np.zeros(nvox,dtype=float); sigvals[sig]=t[sig]; sigmap=full_img(sigvals,fill=0)\nplotting.plot_stat_map(sigmap,display_mode='z',cut_coords=[-8,-4,0,4],threshold=0,cmap='Reds',\n                       colorbar=True,title='Positive voxels surviving whole-brain Bonferroni FWE (p<.05)',\n                       output_file=str(FIG/'whole_brain_fwe.png'))\n# Keep a combined overview under the report's primary figure name.\nfrom PIL import Image\nleft=Image.open(FIG/'group_mean_cope.png').convert('RGB'); right=Image.open(FIG/'whole_brain_fwe.png').convert('RGB')\nh=max(left.height,right.height); left=left.resize((round(left.width*h/left.height),h)); right=right.resize((round(right.width*h/right.height),h))\ncanvas=Image.new('RGB',(left.width+right.width,h),'white'); canvas.paste(left,(0,0)); canvas.paste(right,(left.width,0)); canvas.save(FIG/'whole_brain_results.png')\n# Figure 2: participant-level broad vmPFC proxy average and mean CI.\nfig,ax=plt.subplots(figsize=(7,4.5))\nax.scatter(np.arange(1,N+1),roi_subj,s=24,color='#285f8f',alpha=.82)\nax.axhline(0,color='black',lw=1)\nax.axhline(roi_mean,color='#c33',lw=2,label=f'Mean={roi_mean:.3f}; 95% CI [{roi_ci[0]:.3f}, {roi_ci[1]:.3f}]')\nax.fill_between([0,N+1],roi_ci[0],roi_ci[1],color='#c33',alpha=.12)\nax.set(xlim=(0,N+1),xlabel='Participant (sorted by source table order)',ylabel='Mean COPE in atlas vmPFC proxy',title='Participant-level anatomical summary')\nax.legend(frameon=False); fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(FIG/'vmPFC_proxy_participants.png',dpi=180); plt.close(fig)\nprint(json.dumps(summary,indent=2))\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Restore only the 54 fixed participant COPE maps listed in input/sources.json.\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport concurrent.futures, hashlib, json, urllib.request\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nmanifest=json.loads((ROOT/'input'/'sources.json').read_text())['files']\nitems=[(ROOT/key,meta) for key,meta in manifest.items() if key.startswith('data/')]\nif len(items)!=54:\n    raise RuntimeError(f'Expected 54 participant maps, found {len(items)}')\ndef restore(item):\n    path,meta=item\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\n    if path.is_symlink() and not path.exists():\n        path.unlink()  # replace a broken git-annex pointer in the supplied workspace\n    if path.exists():\n        raw=path.read_bytes()\n        if len(raw)==meta['bytes'] and hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()==meta['sha256']:\n            return path.name,'verified existing'\n    request=urllib.request.Request(meta['url'],headers={'User-Agent':'NARPS-group-analysis/1.0'})\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(request,timeout=90) as response:\n        raw=response.read()\n    digest=hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()\n    if len(raw)!=meta['bytes'] or digest!=meta['sha256']:\n        raise ValueError(f'Checksum/size mismatch for {path.name}')\n    path.write_bytes(raw)\n    return path.name,'downloaded and verified'\nwith concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=6) as pool:\n    for name,status in pool.map(restore,items): print(status,name)\n# Fixed upstream analysis\n\nEach map is one participant's unthresholded gain-effect estimate from NARPS team AO86, averaged across four runs.\nThe 54 participants comprise the complete equal-indifference group in OpenNeuro ds001734 version 1.0.4.\nThese are effect estimates, not standardized test statistics or group results.\nMaps are reported in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space.\n\nAO86 used fMRIPrep outputs and nistats participant models.\nTheir reported gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution; its coefficients must not be interpreted as change per currency unit.\nResponse trials used response-time durations, with separate response-choice and gain modulators.\nNonresponse trials, motion terms, flagged volumes and drift terms were also modeled; runs were combined within participant.\nGain and loss used separate models, so the supplied gain effect is conditional on that modeling choice.\n\nThe reported upstream choices are fixed for this task.\nParticipant variance maps and a complete executable upstream pipeline are not supplied; account for these limits when choosing and interpreting group inference.\n`participants.tsv` retains the source group, age and gender columns.\n`sources.json` identifies each original image, its retrieved-byte checksum, the pinned cohort table and the original methods report.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'set +e\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" probes \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" -o \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/probes/probes.json\" --response \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response-draft.json\" --kind study > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.stderr\"\nrc=$?\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$rc\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.exit\"\ncat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.stderr\"; printf '\"'exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$rc\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/probes/probes.json\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'set +e\n\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" probes \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET\" -o \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/probes/probes.json\" --response \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/response-draft.json\" --kind study > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.stdout\" 2> \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.stderr\"\nrc=$?\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$rc\" > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.exit\"\ncat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.stdout\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/probes.stderr\"; printf '\"'exit=%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$rc\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/probes/probes.json\"'","aggregated_output":"probe                    status          items\nci-present               not-checked     should/002, should/006\nclone-weight             met             (extra)\nderived-have-records     not-applicable  must/006\nentry-point              unmet           must/007, must/008\nenv-spec-tracked         unmet           must/010, must/013, must/016\ninputs-untouched         not-applicable  (extra)\nlarge-in-annex           met             must/005\nlicense-declared         unmet           (extra)\nmodules-separated        partial         should/003\nno-abs-paths             met             must/009\nplatform-assumptions     not-checked     must/011, must/012\nrun-env-linked           not-checked     must/006, must/015\nsubdatasets-resolvable   not-checked     must/002, may/001\ntree-clean               unmet           must/004\n\nprobes cover 13/17 MUST items; inspect statuses for completed verdicts\n\nwrote /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-16-j01/attempt-01/judgment/probes/probes.json\nwrote /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-