rker’s report/scripts and can use the declared route can retrieve the 54 participant COPE maps using `analysis/restore_maps.py` and `input/sources.json`, which point to NeuroVault and validate each expected byte count and SHA-256. HTTP HEAD checks to all 54 declared map URLs succeeded at assessment time (host scope: `neurovault.org`); no payload was fetched during the access check. This tests availability of the map artifacts only. No worker-declared route was found that publishes or provides access to the complete report, code, results and environment as a research object. Coordinator delivery to the assessor is not evidence that the worker had published the complete object. The detailed access record is `access-record.json`.\n\n**Replay: not checked.** The report documents `python analysis/restore_maps.py` followed by `python analysis/group_analysis.py`; the latter generates the outputs named in its code under `results/` and `figures/`. However, the worker supplied no dependency/environment declaration. The analysis imports NumPy, pandas, nibabel, SciPy, nilearn, Matplotlib and Pillow and fetches an atlas at runtime. The report’s mention of Python 3.13 does not specify or pin these dependencies or the atlas resource. Under the scope rule, I did not invent an environment or run the code with assessor-installed dependencies. No replay attempt was made, no shipped outputs are treated as replay evidence, and no target files were altered. `replay-record.json` records the reason and the documented commands/output selection.\n\n## Item-level summary\n\n- **Met:** must/001, must/002, must/008, must/009, should/003, may/002, may/003, may/004, may/005, should/001.\n- **Unmet:** must/003, must/004, must/005, must/006, must/007, must/010–017, should/005, should/007, should/008.\n- **Not checked:** should/002, should/004, should/006.\n- **Not applicable:** should/009, may/001.\n\nThe complete response JSON provides each item’s rationale and capture-cited evidence. The generated checklist URL is in `checklist-link.txt`.\nEOF\ncat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/replay-record.json\" <<'\"'EOF'\n{\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"not-checked\\\",\n  \\\"attempts\\\": 0,\n  \\\"maximum_attempts\\\": 1,\n  \\\"execution_limit_seconds\\\": 7200,\n  \\\"source\\\": \\\"canonical original complete delivery\\\",\n  \\\"documented_entrypoint\\\": [\\\"python analysis/restore_maps.py\\\", \\\"python analysis/group_analysis.py\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\": {\n    \\\"documented\\\": [\\\"Python 3.13 (report.md)\\\"],\n    \\\"missing\\\": [\\\"dependency specification or lock\\\", \\\"pinned/captured Harvard-Oxford atlas resource\\\"],\n    \\\"reason\\\": \\\"The worker did not supply a dependency declaration. The group script imports NumPy, pandas, nibabel, SciPy, nilearn, Matplotlib and Pillow and fetches an atlas at runtime. Reconstructing those from assessor environment state would exceed the supplied instructions/declarations.\\\"\n  },\n  \\\"scientific_output_selection\\\": [\n    \\\"results/map_qc.csv\\\",\n    \\\"results/group_mean_cope.nii.gz\\\",\n    \\\"results/group_t_positive.nii.gz\\\",\n    \\\"results/group_neglog10_p_bonferroni.nii.gz\\\",\n    \\\"results/summary.json\\\",\n    \\\"results/fwe_positive_voxels.csv\\\",\n    \\\"results/vmPFC_proxy_participant_estimates.csv\\\",\n    \\\"figures/group_mean_cope.png\\\",\n    \\\"figures/whole_brain_fwe.png\\\",\n    \\\"figures/whole_brain_results.png\\\",\n    \\\"figures/vmPFC_proxy_participants.png\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"comparison_rule_if_run\\\": \\\"Compare reported scientific numeric quantities and map values at rtol=1e-6; separate timestamps, logs, prose, formatting, atlas/version changes and stochastic/numerical differences. No replay was attempted, so no comparison was made.\\\",\n  \\\"input_protection\\\": \\\"No replay copy was created because required environment reconstruction could not be established. No source inputs or target files were changed by a replay.\\\",\n  \\\"attempts_re