{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '27,60p' \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/assessment-report.md\";'","aggregated_output":"**Recipient and tested route:** a researcher who has the worker’s report/scripts and can use the declared route can retrieve the 54 participant COPE maps using `analysis/restore_maps.py` and `input/sources.json`, which point to NeuroVault and validate each expected byte count and SHA-256. HTTP HEAD checks to all 54 declared map URLs succeeded at assessment time (host scope: `neurovault.org`); no payload was fetched during the access check. This tests availability of the map artifacts only. No worker-declared route was found that publishes or provides access to the complete report, code, results and environment as a research object. Coordinator delivery to the assessor is not evidence that the worker had published the complete object. The detailed access record is `access-record.json`. Target evidence: `content/workspace/analysis/restore_maps.py` (capture SHA-256 `1bc0f46ef4ad58e9f70bb654d761eb330f15d1c87929ad165d414907dd7d0f68`; path SHA-256 `f85d8e254b7ddee23a041aa0be22964260c059132fe6294424c42152eb39e3ea`) and `content/workspace/input/sources.json` (same capture SHA; path SHA-256 `919be9b4278c31f7e39ae3d02fcf159eb4ae222a2fb96c90df7c3a92e5fb19cd`).\n\n**Replay: not checked.** The report documents `python analysis/restore_maps.py` followed by `python analysis/group_analysis.py`; the latter generates the outputs named in its code under `results/` and `figures/`. However, the worker supplied no dependency/environment declaration. The analysis imports NumPy, pandas, nibabel, SciPy, nilearn, Matplotlib and Pillow and fetches an atlas at runtime. The report’s mention of Python 3.13 does not specify or pin these dependencies or the atlas resource. Under the scope rule, I did not invent an environment or run the code with assessor-installed dependencies. No replay attempt was made, no shipped outputs are treated as replay evidence, and no target files were altered. `replay-record.json` records the reason and the documented commands/output selection.\n\n## Item-level summary\n\n- **Met:** must/001, must/002, must/008, must/009, may/002, may/003, may/004, may/005.\n- **Unmet:** must/003, must/004, must/005, must/006, must/007, must/010–017, should/001, should/005, should/007, should/008.\n- **Not checked:** should/002, should/004, should/006. Partial: should/003.\n- \n\nThe item summary below includes only findings recorded before the response action failed. Later items are listed as unavailable in both the formal response and this report; they are not scored. The checklist URL was not generated.\n\n\nThe worker’s verbatim hypothesis conclusion is: “The supplied equal-indifference group maps do **not support** the prediction of a positive vmPFC gain effect under whole-brain family-wise error control.”\n\n**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The group model and whole-brain corrected absence support the report’s bounded no-support conclusion; the result does not establish a zero effect.\n\n## Assessor malfunction and response status\n\nThe frozen runner’s response-set action failed while setting `should/009`, reporting that its recorded local environment file had changed. The first two recorded response attempts also stopped on item-reason length limits; those failed attempts are preserved separately. The final failed command, stdout, stderr and exit code are retained under `commands/response-set-should-009.*`; no retry or replacement assessor was used. The required frozen response validation was attempted and failed because assessor metadata fields were null/empty in the partial response. The response therefore remains incomplete and invalid; subsequent item measures are unavailable in that formal response. This malfunction is separate from target behavior and does not alter the scientific assessment above. No checklist-app URL was generated.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'python - \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\" <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,sys,hashlib\nout=Path(sys.argv[1]); p=out/'assessment-report.md'; t=p.read_text()\nt=t.replace('- **Unmet:** must/003, must/004, must/005, must/006, must/007, must/010–017, should/001, should/005, should/007, should/008.','- **Unmet:** must/003, must/004, must/005, must/006, must/007, must/010–017, should/001.')\nt=t.replace('- **Not checked:** should/002, should/004, should/006. Partial: should/003.\\\\n-','- **Not checked:** should/002. **Partial:** should/003.\\\\n- **Unavailable after assessor malfunction:** should/009, should/004–008, may/001–005. These remain not-checked in \"'`response.json`; no post-failure verdict was substituted.'\"')\np.write_text(t)\nlines=t.splitlines()\ndef ex(q):\n for i,l in enumerate(lines,1):\n  if q in l:return {'quote':q,'start_line':i,'end_line':i}\n raise ValueError(q)\nrec={'schema_version':1,'delivery_capture_sha256':'1bc0f46ef4ad58e9f70bb654d761eb330f15d1c87929ad165d414907dd7d0f68','scientific_adequacy':'supported','report':{'path':'assessment-report.md','sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()},'adequacy_evidence':ex('**Scientific adequacy: supported.** The group model and whole-brain corrected absence support the report’s bounded no-support conclusion; the result does not establish a zero effect.'),'hypothesis_conclusion':ex('The supplied equal-indifference group maps do **not support** the prediction of a positive vmPFC gain effect under whole-brain family-wise error control.')}\n(out/'scientific-judgment.json').write_text(json.dumps(rec,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\ncat > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/initial-runner-check-record.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Initial frozen runner check (required preflight)\n\nCommand: \"'`\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" check`\n\nObserved result on the initial preflight: exit 0; stdout began `✔ The default environment has been installed.` and printed assessment version 1, source commit `9852d8360f9519d21d11099b45f5deb8ba80cb28`, environment commit `3552d5003a2485b6405805236d5c54e7ed42f097`, and the pinned `pixi.toml`/`pixi.lock` SHA-256 values in `assessment-version.json`. No stderr was observed. The initial shell call was not redirected at the time; this record preserves the observed output and is distinguished from the separately captured final check in `runner-check-final.*`.\nEOF\ncat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/finalize-pass-01.stdout\" <<'\"'EOF'\nFAILED must/004 1 ✔ The default environment has been installed.\nwarning: responses/stamped-checklist:must/004/reason: 'At worker stop the analysis scripts, report, figures and result files were untracked; the captured HEAD is the supplied-inputs commit, not a worker commit for these deliverables. Operational Git status is an assessor observation, not itself worker evidence.' is too long\nwarning: stamped-checklist:must/004: reason is 257 chars; the app truncates at 250\nEOF\n: > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/finalize-pass-01.stderr\"\necho 1 > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/finalize-pass-01.exit\"\ncat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/finalize-pass-02.stdout\" <<'\"'EOF'\nFAILED must/005 1 ✔ The default environment has been installed.\nwarning: responses/stamped-checklist:must/005/reason: 'The 54 large maps were materialized as regular files at worker stop and operational Git status showed tracked annex symlinks type-changed. The annex-backed pointers/objects are inherited capture material and are not credited as a worker annex publication.' is too long\nwarning: stamped-checklist:must/005: reason is 255 chars; the app truncates at 250\nEOF\n: > \\\"\"'$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/finalize-pass-02.stderr\"\necho 1 > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/finalize-pass-02.exit\"\ncat > \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT/commands/assessor-action-attempt-ledger.md\" <<'\"'EOF'\n# Failed frozen response-action attempts\n\n1. Response finalization attempt 1 reached \"'`must/004`; frozen response action exited 1 because the reason length was 257 characters (maximum 250). Exact observed stdout/stderr/exit are in `finalize-pass-01.*`.\n2. Attempt 2 reached `must/005`; frozen response action exited 1 because the reason length was 255 characters. Exact observed stdout/stderr/exit are in `finalize-pass-02.*`.\n3. Attempt 3 reached `should/009`; frozen response action exited 1 with `Recorded environment was changed locally: .../assessment-runtime/3552d5003a2485b6405805236d5c54e7ed42f097/pixi.toml`. The corresponding per-item argv/stdout/stderr/exit files are `response-set-should-009.*`.\n\nThe first two item-reason attempts were shortened only to fit the frozen response schema; the third failure was not retried. No environment repair or alternate response writer was used.\nEOF\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
